# Line endings that must not depend on the machine that checked the repository out.
#
# Migration files are checksummed (SHA-256 of their bytes) and the checksum is verified on every
# boot. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to CRLF, which changes the bytes,
# which changes the checksum — so a database created on a Mac would refuse to start under a binary
# built on Windows from the "same" source. Pinning LF makes the checksum a property of the
# repository rather than of the checkout.
*.sql  text eol=lf

# Embedded catalogs are compared byte-for-byte by nothing today, but they are go:embed'd into the
# binary and imported by Vite, and one set of bytes for both is the point of sharing them.
*.json text eol=lf

# A shell script with CRLF fails under Git Bash with "$'\r': command not found".
*.sh   text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be normalised.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
